WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:18.786
"Can you really fix my bike?" Nathan asked Tina. "Thanks!"

2
00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:23.495
"You're welcome. This will only take a second."

3
00:00:23.496 --> 00:00:27.725
Tina bent over the bike and expertly put the chain back in place.

4
00:00:27.726 --> 00:00:30.543
Then she turned the pedals to test it.

5
00:00:30.544 --> 00:00:35.388
"Good as new," she said. "It should be fine now."

6
00:00:35.389 --> 00:00:41.553
"Thank you so much!" Nathan exclaimed. "I really appreciate it."

7
00:00:41.554 --> 00:00:46.710
"No problem. Enjoy the rest of the ride!"

8
00:00:46.711 --> 00:00:50.556
With a friendly wave to all of them, Tina pedaled off.

9
00:00:50.557 --> 00:00:55.198
"Wow," Maggie said. "That was really nice of her."

10
00:00:55.199 --> 00:01:00.238
Cole nodded. "Yeah, and she's one of our suspects," he said.

11
00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:04.996
"Would someone who just slashed a bunch of tires do something nice like that?"

12
00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:09.888
"I'm glad you guys are trying to figure out who slashed those tires," Nathan said.

13
00:01:09.889 --> 00:01:13.301
"That means it won't be long until the mystery is solved.

14
00:01:13.302 --> 00:01:17.539
The Lemonade Detectives solve all their cases!"

15
00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.850
He rode off, humming happily.

16
00:01:19.851 --> 00:01:23.019
Henry frowned, realizing that Nathan was right.

17
00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:28.143
"It's true," he said. "We've solved every case so far.

18
00:01:28.144 --> 00:01:31.414
But this one might be our toughest yet."

19
00:01:31.415 --> 00:01:34.362
Maggie looked worried. "You're right.

20
00:01:34.363 --> 00:01:37.600
What if we can't solve it before the ride is over?

21
00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:41.325
The Lemonade Detectives' reputation will be ruined!"

22
00:01:41.326 --> 00:01:46.773
"And so will the soccer team's fundraiser," Cole said. "But don't worry.

23
00:01:46.774 --> 00:01:50.611
We already have it narrowed down to three suspects, remember?"

24
00:01:50.612 --> 00:01:56.607
"Or maybe two," Henry said. "It's hard to believe Tina is the culprit.

25
00:01:56.608 --> 00:01:58.831
She seems too nice.

26
00:01:58.832 --> 00:02:04.161
And she seemed pretty mad when she accused Joey of slashing the tires earlier."

27
00:02:04.162 --> 00:02:08.369
"But why would she help raise money for Belltown?" Maggie said.

28
00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.620
"That doesn't make sense."

29
00:02:10.621 --> 00:02:13.236
"I don't know," Henry said.

30
00:02:13.237 --> 00:02:16.750
"But I know someone who might be able to tell us.

31
00:02:16.751 --> 00:02:22.163
I just remembered I saw Tina sitting with Daisy for a while during the break."

32
00:02:22.164 --> 00:02:25.949
"Oh yeah, I noticed that too," Cole said.

33
00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:31.498
"I was surprised that Tina wasn't sitting with that Joey guy since they're both from Valley High.

34
00:02:31.499 --> 00:02:34.470
Do you think Tina and Daisy are friends?"

35
00:02:34.471 --> 00:02:40.558
"There's only one way to find out," Henry replied. "Let's go ask Daisy."

36
00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:46.876
They rode ahead until they caught up with Daisy.

37
00:02:46.877 --> 00:02:49.763
Maggie jumped right into questioning her.

38
00:02:49.764 --> 00:02:54.279
"We saw you sitting with that girl from Valley High earlier," she said to Daisy.

39
00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.982
"Do you know her?"

40
00:02:55.983 --> 00:02:58.513
"You mean Tina?" Daisy nodded.

41
00:02:58.514 --> 00:03:03.320
"We went to the same summer camp last year. She's cool."

42
00:03:03.321 --> 00:03:06.543
"Is that why she came on this ride?" Cole asked.

43
00:03:06.544 --> 00:03:08.618
"Because you two are friends?"

44
00:03:08.619 --> 00:03:13.007
Daisy shrugged. "I'm the one who told her about the fundraiser.

45
00:03:13.008 --> 00:03:16.372
But she probably would have heard about it anyway.

46
00:03:16.373 --> 00:03:18.833
She's a really serious rider.

47
00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:25.084
She trains all the time, and she enters every local ride and race she can find."

48
00:03:25.085 --> 00:03:29.259
"Oh, that explains why she's here!" Henry said.

49
00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:32.914
"It also explains how she knew how to fix Nathan's bike."

50
00:03:32.915 --> 00:03:35.608
"Wait a minute," Daisy said.

51
00:03:35.609 --> 00:03:39.824
"You don't suspect Tina of slashing those tires, do you?

52
00:03:39.825 --> 00:03:42.707
Because she'd never do something like that.

53
00:03:42.708 --> 00:03:46.798
She loves bikes, plus she's really nice."

54
00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:50.695
"Yeah. We just figured that out." Henry smiled.

55
00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:54.769
"Don't worry. She's off our list of suspects."

56
00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:58.848
He, Maggie, and Cole rode off by themselves.

57
00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:05.735
"So now we only have two suspects," Cole said. "William and the mystery man."

58
00:04:05.736 --> 00:04:10.475
"Both of them have been acting suspicious all day," Maggie said.

59
00:04:10.476 --> 00:04:13.985
"But neither has a good motive," Henry pointed out.

60
00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:16.846
"At least not one we know about."

61
00:04:16.847 --> 00:04:20.984
"William isn't having much fun on this ride," Maggie said.

62
00:04:20.985 --> 00:04:23.987
"He acts like he doesn't even want to be here."

63
00:04:23.988 --> 00:04:30.461
"And he tried to convince Ms. Hernandez to let him quit at the first rest break," Cole said.

64
00:04:30.462 --> 00:04:36.174
"Maybe he slashed the tires because he thought the rest of the ride would be canceled.

65
00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:40.741
Then when it wasn't, he had to figure out another way to quit early."

66
00:04:40.742 --> 00:04:45.729
"Why would he come on the ride at all if he didn't want to be here?" Maggie wondered.

67
00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:48.299
"Do you think his parents made him come?"

68
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.131
"I don't know," Henry said.

69
00:04:51.132 --> 00:04:56.435
"But I can't stop thinking about how that guy lied to us about being a reporter.

70
00:04:56.436 --> 00:04:58.791
Why would he do that?"

71
00:04:58.792 --> 00:05:01.424
"Good question," Maggie said.

72
00:05:01.425 --> 00:05:04.523
"I just don't know how we're going to figure it out.

73
00:05:04.524 --> 00:05:10.845
He won't tell us anything. And nobody else here knows anything about him."

74
00:05:10.846 --> 00:05:14.654
Soon they reached the next rest area.

75
00:05:14.655 --> 00:05:19.284
Henry coasted to a stop behind the other bikes.

76
00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:23.762
This picnic area was right beside a parking lot.

77
00:05:23.763 --> 00:05:28.718
That was good since it meant that nobody could touch the bikes without being seen.

78
00:05:28.719 --> 00:05:32.514
"We'd better figure out how to solve this case," Henry said.

79
00:05:32.515 --> 00:05:36.809
"We're almost out of time."
